class.description:
Main interface for working with YAML in Godot, providing methods to parse, validate, and serialize YAML data. [url=https://yaml.org/]YAML (YAML Ain't Markup Language)[/url] is a human-friendly data serialization standard commonly used for configuration files, data exchange, and storing structured information in a readable format. This class automatically handles conversion between YAML and standard Godot variant types, except for [Callable] and [RID]. [b]Basic Usage Example:[/b] [codeblock lang=gdscript] # Parse a YAML string var yaml_text = """ player: name: Knight health: 100 inventory: - Sword - Shield - Health Potion """
var result = YAML.parse(yaml_text) if !result.has_error(): var data = result.get_data() print("Player name: %s" % data.player.name) print("Health: %d" % data.player.health) print("First item: %s" % data.player.inventory[0])
# Convert Godot data to YAML var enemy_data = { "name": "Dragon", "health": 500, "attacks": ["Bite", "Fire Breath", "Tail Whip"] }
var string_result = YAML.stringify(enemy_data) if !string_result.has_error(): print(string_result.get_data()) [/codeblock]

method.description:
Validates YAML syntax without performing a full parse. Faster than [method parse] when you only need to check validity.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var user_input = get_text_from_user()

var result = YAML.validate(user_input)
if result.has_error():
    show_error_message("Invalid YAML: " + result.get_error())
else:
    process_valid_yaml(user_input)
[/codeblock]

Loads and parses a YAML file from the given [param path]. Returns a [YAMLResult] with data or error information.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.load_file("res://data/characters.yaml")
if !result.has_error():
    var characters = result.get_data()
    for character_id in characters:
        var character = characters[character_id]
        add_character_to_world(character)
else:
    push_error("Failed to load characters: " + result.get_error())
[/codeblock]

Converts Godot [param data] to YAML and saves it to a file at [param path]. Returns a [YAMLResult].
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var save_data = {
    "player": {
        "name": "Hero",
        "level": 10,
        "position": [25, 48]
    },
    "quests_completed": ["Rats in the Cellar", "Lost Artifact"]
}

var result = YAML.save_file(save_data, "user://save_game.yaml")
if !result.has_error():
    print("Game saved successfully!")
else:
    push_error("Save failed: " + result.get_error_message())
[/codeblock]

Validates YAML syntax in a file without performing a full parse. Useful for quickly checking file format validity.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.validate_file("user://mod_config.yaml")
if result.has_error():
    print("Mod configuration has syntax errors: " + result.get_error())
    print("Please fix your mod configuration file.")
else:
    print("Mod configuration syntax is valid.")
[/codeblock]

Registers a custom script class for YAML serialization and deserialization.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
# Define a custom Item class
class_name Item extends Resource

var name: String
var weight: float
var value: int

func _init(p_name = "", p_weight = 0.0, p_value = 0):
    name = p_name
    weight = p_weight
    value = p_value

static func deserialize(data):
    if typeof(data) != TYPE_DICTIONARY:
        return YAMLResult.error("Item requires a dictionary")

    return Item.new(
        data.get("name", ""),
        data.get("weight", 0.0),
        data.get("value", 0)
    )

func serialize():
    return {
        "name": name,
        "weight": weight,
        "value": value
    }

# Register the class for YAML serialization
YAML.register_class(Item)

# Now we can serialize/deserialize Item objects
var sword = Item.new("Iron Sword", 5.0, 100)
var result = YAML.stringify(sword)
print(result.get_data())
# Output: !Item {name: Iron Sword, weight: 5.0, value: 100}
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method stringify] that returns the YAML string directly, or an empty string on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var npc = {
    "name": "Merchant",
    "dialog": "Welcome to my shop!",
    "shop_items": ["Potion", "Map", "Torch"]
}

var yaml_text = YAML.try_stringify(npc)
if yaml_text:
    save_to_file(yaml_text)
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method load_file] that returns the parsed data directly, or [code]null[/code] on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var settings = YAML.try_load_file("user://settings.yaml")
if settings:
    apply_settings(settings)
else:
    create_default_settings()
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method save_file] that returns [code]true[/code] on success, [code]false[/code] on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var player_progress = {
    "level_completed": 5,
    "collectibles": 28,
    "unlocked_abilities": ["double_jump", "dash"]
}

if YAML.try_save_file(player_progress, "user://progress.yaml"):
    print("Progress saved!")
else:
    print("Failed to save progress")
[/codeblock]
